WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.640
- Social media is bursting
with cool stories,

00:00:02.640 --> 00:00:04.120
you may miss in this shuffle,

00:00:04.120 --> 00:00:05.930
but I will not let you miss the best.

00:00:05.930 --> 00:00:07.326
This is what I'm liking.

00:00:07.326 --> 00:00:10.460
(crowd cheering)

00:00:10.460 --> 00:00:13.700
This one speaks to what the
New York spirit is all about.

00:00:13.700 --> 00:00:16.510
When "Fat Bike" Phil came
across an abandoned guitar,

00:00:16.510 --> 00:00:18.480
near a pile of trash in hell's kitchen,

00:00:18.480 --> 00:00:21.200
he was sure no one would
intentionally throw it away.

00:00:21.200 --> 00:00:22.380
He looked inside

00:00:22.380 --> 00:00:25.870
and found it had the name of
the owner, Daniel Martinez.

00:00:25.870 --> 00:00:28.220
So, "Fat Bike" Phil set out on a mission.

00:00:28.220 --> 00:00:31.090
He hoisted the guitar on
his back, pedaled at home,

00:00:31.090 --> 00:00:32.930
and set out to find Daniel.

00:00:32.930 --> 00:00:35.420
With some great detective
work, he figured it out.

00:00:35.420 --> 00:00:37.620
But that's just where the story begins.

00:00:37.620 --> 00:00:40.040
We have "Fat Bike" Phil
and Daniel on the line.

00:00:40.040 --> 00:00:42.840
What's up gentlemen?
(crowd cheering)

00:00:42.840 --> 00:00:45.340
- Hey Kelly.
- Hi, how are you?

00:00:46.284 --> 00:00:50.233
- So, Phil, you found the
guitar just in time, right?

00:00:51.070 --> 00:00:53.640
- Kelly, it had been raining
like crazy in the city

00:00:53.640 --> 00:00:55.630
and I was out on my bike.

00:00:55.630 --> 00:00:58.554
And I'm riding around during
the break in the rain.

00:00:58.554 --> 00:01:02.260
I saw this guitar case leaning
against the scaffolding

00:01:02.260 --> 00:01:04.240
next to this huge pile of garbage.

00:01:04.240 --> 00:01:06.940
And so, I went and I investigated.

00:01:06.940 --> 00:01:07.773
I looked inside

00:01:07.773 --> 00:01:10.580
and I saw that there was an
acoustic guitar in there.

00:01:10.580 --> 00:01:11.550
And I don't know,

00:01:11.550 --> 00:01:14.390
just the guitar player in
me couldn't abandon it.

00:01:14.390 --> 00:01:18.050
So, I put it on my back
and took it back with me,

00:01:18.050 --> 00:01:19.390
and opened it up,

00:01:19.390 --> 00:01:23.120
and realized this is a
very expensive guitar.

00:01:23.120 --> 00:01:25.530
Somebody is crushed right now.

00:01:25.530 --> 00:01:27.430
I called up my wife on the phone

00:01:27.430 --> 00:01:30.900
and we found some stuff
in the guitar case.

00:01:30.900 --> 00:01:31.733
I called her up.

00:01:31.733 --> 00:01:32.640
We did some sleuthing,

00:01:32.640 --> 00:01:36.690
and we found Daniel on Facebook
playing that same guitar.

00:01:36.690 --> 00:01:38.709
So, we knew we had our guy.

00:01:38.709 --> 00:01:40.979
- Aw, man.
(crowd cheering)

00:01:40.979 --> 00:01:44.515
Well, Daniel, that guitar
means the world to you, right?

00:01:44.515 --> 00:01:46.182
So, how do you feel?

00:01:47.187 --> 00:01:48.703
- I feel grateful.

00:01:48.703 --> 00:01:53.390
I feel fortune because
the guitar is like a part

00:01:53.390 --> 00:01:55.030
or extension of your body.

00:01:55.030 --> 00:01:57.330
So, even if I get another guitar,

00:01:57.330 --> 00:01:58.620
it's never going to be the same.

00:01:58.620 --> 00:02:02.060
It's like, if a part of you is cut out.

00:02:02.060 --> 00:02:03.830
Even if you replaced it,

00:02:03.830 --> 00:02:05.200
it's not gonna be the same.

00:02:05.200 --> 00:02:06.870
So, I feel good.

00:02:06.870 --> 00:02:07.940
I feel grateful.

00:02:07.940 --> 00:02:10.110
And when I met Phil,

00:02:10.110 --> 00:02:13.740
it was amazing that he was a musician too.

00:02:13.740 --> 00:02:18.180
So, God is good all the time.
(Kelly laughs)

00:02:18.180 --> 00:02:19.760
I feel grateful.

00:02:19.760 --> 00:02:21.290
- I would watch this show by the way.

00:02:21.290 --> 00:02:23.970
You two are awesome
together. (everyone laughs)

00:02:23.970 --> 00:02:26.920
So wait, Phil and Daniel, can
you play a little for us now?

00:02:27.821 --> 00:02:28.654
- Of course, yes.

00:02:28.654 --> 00:02:30.426
- Danny, let's do something
in A minor. Ready?

00:02:30.426 --> 00:02:33.142
- Okay.
- One, two, three, let's go.

00:02:33.142 --> 00:02:36.475
(mellow acoustic music)

00:02:44.125 --> 00:02:47.821
- Yeah!
(crowd cheering)

00:02:47.821 --> 00:02:49.443
Oh my God, I love that.

00:02:49.443 --> 00:02:52.141
Thank you so much, Phil and Daniel.

00:02:52.141 --> 00:02:55.760
I'm liking your post right now, all right.

00:02:55.760 --> 00:02:56.810
All right, well, that's not all.

00:02:56.810 --> 00:02:58.560
Our season long partner, Pilot Pen,

00:02:58.560 --> 00:03:00.470
the go to pen at the Kelly Clarkson show,

00:03:00.470 --> 00:03:03.510
thinks that your story is
as incredible as we do.

00:03:03.510 --> 00:03:06.540
And in recognition, they'd
like to write you each a check

00:03:06.540 --> 00:03:09.550
with their G2 gel ink pen for $500.

00:03:09.550 --> 00:03:11.600
Together, that's a $1,000.

00:03:11.600 --> 00:03:13.880
All just for you.
(crowd cheering)

00:03:13.880 --> 00:03:14.861
- [Daniel] Thank you.

00:03:14.861 --> 00:03:16.387
- [Kelly] Thank you guys so much.

